  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 211 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThursday evening starts of this long term period with monsoonal \nmoisture moving in, and a shortwave moving through the area. With \nprecipitable water values in the 1-1.5 range, RH values 60-90%, and \nthe shortwave, its safe to say our area will be getting some much \nneeded moisture. This moisture sticks around through Monday, \nbringing daily afternoon chances of precipitation. This \nprecipitation looks to mainly be showers, but an isolated \nthunderstorm cannot be ruled out especially near the NE panhandle \nwith CAPE values near 1000J/kg. Winds do not appear to be out of the \nordinary, staying below 15 knots most of the time. Temperatures cool \noff as a cold front moves over the area Thursday. 700mb temperatures \nstay near 12C during the daytime Thursday-Sunday, with nighttime \ntemperatures getting near 10C. This means temperatures will cool off \nnearly 20F from what we have been experiencing. Typically our area \nhas daytime temperatures near 83F this time of year. This is a \nwelcomed break from our hot temperatures the last few weeks. With \nall of this monsoonal moisture coming in, fire weather is not a \nconcern through this long term period.&&",
